meta {
  name: List sessions filtered by range and status
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sessions?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31&status=finished,abandoned
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200 [{ "id": 15, "date": "2026-10-10", "status": "finished" }]

  Range and status combine. Rows are still geometry-free (see
  list-sessions.bru); status is filtered after deriveStatus runs, so a
  session that only BECOMES finished because its boats uploaded runs
  appears here without any extra query.

  The Sessions pane filters client-side today — the calendar day counts
  need the unfiltered set — so these params are the API surface for
  paging later, not something the UI currently sends.

  400 when from > to, a date is malformed, or a status is not one of
  scheduled/live/finished/abandoned.
}